Release 3.7.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 10:42:37

Fixed. The text of the wiki chapter and of the window now follows the suite's writing standard. Its sentences are short,
with one fact each. The wiki chapter now uses lists for the values the app shows, the problems a drive can flag, what
stays empty over USB, what to try on a slow USB link and the drives left out of the rated list. The info text and the
tooltips of Screenshot, the Test pill, Board link and No SMART over USB now use whole sentences. So do the advice for a
slow USB link, the firmware update tooltip and the messages for a missing busctl, a missing firmware list and too little
free space. No labels were renamed. The info text now writes the Health box's “Not reported” with a capital N, as the
window shows it. The speed test's file is 1 GiB and its space check needs 2 GiB, so the wiki and the tooltip now say
about 1 GB and about 2 GB. Nothing the app does has changed. No tests changed.

